 "notes": [
  "POST-HOC ABLATION (not a decision): no hardening / pre-submission / G2 / G8 rule or configuration is changed by these numbers.",
  "Candidate set = HRCOV bridge-free (HRCOV_PAT, W 100) on all four bases; arms change feature columns only; fusion alpha*log p + beta*f calibrated on valid-select for every arm; seeds 0-2; all test queries (polecat 532,636; smallpedia 163,172).",
  "A11 'minus base' is the same column subset as A10 and is reported once (A10_noBase).",
  "Evaluator: smallpedia arms scored by the official py-tgb 2.3.0 Evaluator on CPU (serverA); harness-minus-official MRR <= 2.3e-7 for every arm. Polecat arms use the exact fused rank (1 + #greater + 0.5 #ties over the non-filtered entities = the evaluator's statistic) because the official evaluator needs full polecat base rows, which exist only via GPU replay of TiRGN / LogCL (not allowed in this CPU-only add-on). Validation: the polecat TiRGN FULL arm reproduces the stored official HRCOV_PAT MRR exactly (0.2823777), and on the official HRCOV_PAT lists of polecat LogCL / TiRGN and smallpedia TiRGN the exact rank and the official evaluator agree to |dMRR| <= 8.4e-8.",
  "FULL arms were re-trained on serverA CPU (8 threads); the decision HRCOV_PAT runs for polecat LogCL / smallpedia TiRGN / regcn_tgb were trained on GPU and differ by <= 1.6e-4 MRR (device numerics).",
